<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5023" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bassăreus</span></b> , ei,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βασσαρεύς</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασσάρα</span>, a fox, fox-skin, as clothing of the
		Bacchantes], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a title
				of Bacchus</i>: candide Bassareu, * Hor C. 1, 18, 11;
			cf. <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 18</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bassărĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of Bacchus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comae,</span>”
				<i>the hair of Bacchus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				3</span></i>
			 (4), 17, 30: metrum, Mar. Vict. p. 2545
			P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bassăris</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βασσαρίς</span>, <i>a
			Bacchante</i>, <i><span class="en">Pers. 1, 101</span></i> Schol.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
